      "explainer": "This number represents baseline deaths in areas prior to VAS campaigns, so mortality rates should be lower in areas where campaigns are currently occuring. On the other hand, it is possible that mortality rates are higher for those harder-to-reach populations regardless of the existence of VAS campaigns. We assume as a rough guess that these two effects cancel each other out. GiveWell estimate.\n\nSource: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1k2OwWwa9F4RtY_7mEwjoDtq2TeZvR_SHDW216T9TVis/edit#gid=0&range=K18"
